    {
      "added_at": "2026-11-14T20:09:27.063792+00:00",
      "amendment_id": "A2-coverage-denominator",
      "note": "Coverage = usable keys / expected keys. Expected keys of a model: every covered municipality (catalog coverage, the model scope states and, for candidates, the artifact coverage) x cutoff of the harvest whose planned issue date (cutoff date + 6-day lag) is on or after the Brasilia day of the model registration. Usable = on-time record, provenance accepted, non-null estimate.",
      "eligibility_impact": "missing records (job not run, inputs incomplete, not ready), late records, provenance rejections and model errors now count against coverage; before, the denominator was only records already containing the model"
    },
    {
      "added_at": "2026-11-14T20:09:27.075551+00:00",
      "amendment_id": "A3-priority-states",
      "note": "A priority state of the scope (MG and MT for soy/maize2 MG+MT, MG for MG coffee, ES for conilon) with no paired harvest makes the scope result inconclusive; approval is blocked for that scope.",
      "eligibility_impact": "before, a priority state without pairs passed the state check silently"
    },
    {
      "added_at": "2026-11-14T20:09:27.089175+00:00",
      "amendment_id": "A4-provenance",
      "note": "A record enters an approval decision only if: (i) the hash chain of all sealed batches is intact; (ii) its protocol_sha256 is in data/frozen/prospective_v9_protocol_versions.jsonl with a version time not after issued_at; (iii) provenance of NASA POWER, IMERG Late and IBGE PAM is present; (iv) every used input has a retrieval time not after issued_at; (v) availability is proven: the retrieval time was recorded at retrieval (retrieved_at_basis = recorded), or the sealed batch holding the record was committed no later than the day after decision_at. Version hashes are of the protocol file bytes as written (CRLF on the registry machine).",
      "eligibility_impact": "first batch (2026-11-14): POWER and IMERG retrieval times come from cache file times (no sidecar yet); the batch was committed the same day (abb7381, 2026-11-14 16:47 -03), so (v) holds through sealing; records with a missing source or a retrieval after issue are rejected"
    },
    {
      "added_at": "2026-11-14T20:09:27.108446+00:00",
      "amendment_id": "A5-dates",
      "note": "All dates are Brasilia calendar days (UTC-03:00, no daylight saving): cutoff_date = sowing or coffee production-year start + cutoff_days - 1; planned_issue = cutoff_date + 6 (operational data lag); deadline = planned_issue + 7 (tolerance of A1); issued_date = Brasilia day of issued_at, which must equal decision_at. On time: issued_date <= deadline. The registry refuses an as_of different from the Brasilia day of the run.",
      "eligibility_impact": "first batch re-counted with this rule: 244 on time (soy 84 and maize1 160, cutoff 2026-11-03, deadline 2026-11-16) and 1,673 late; an earlier statement that all were late was wrong; no record was rewritten and the tolerance was not changed"
    },
    {
      "added_at": "2026-11-14T20:09:27.134444+00:00",
      "amendment_id": "A6-calendar",
      "note": "The first scoring is expected after the official release of PAM 2027 (IBGE calendar; historically September of the following year, so around September 2028); the date is conditional on that release.",
      "eligibility_impact": "none"
    }
  ]
}
